<h1>double hashing</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A method of <a href="openAddressing.html"><em>open addressing</em></a> for a <a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a> in which a <a href="collision.html"><em>collision</em></a> is resolved by searching the table for an empty place at intervals given by a different hash function, thus minimizing <a href="clustering.html"><em>clustering</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> rehashing.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="linearprobng.html"><em>linear probing</em></a>, <a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Since a different hashing function is used to find a location in case of collision, colliding values should be spread out.  In <a href="linearprobng.html"><em>linear probing</em></a>, <a href="primaryClustering.html"><em>primary clustering</em></a> occurs when collisions fill up every space for long stretches.  Even in <a href="quadraticprb.html"><em>quadratic probing</em></a>, <a href="secondaryClustering.html"><em>secondary clustering</em></a> may develop since colliding values follow the same <a href="probesequenc.html"><em>probe sequence</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
